  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed with する to mean \"to refuel.\" Applies to cars, aircraft, and other fuel-powered vehicles. At self-service gas stations, you may see {給油|きゅうゆ}ランプ (fuel warning light) or セルフ{給油|きゅうゆ} (self-service refueling).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {給油|きゅうゆ}する (to refuel)\n- {給油|きゅうゆ}ランプ (low fuel warning light)\n- セルフ{給油|きゅうゆ} (self-service refueling)\n- {給油|きゅうゆ}{口|ぐち} (fuel filler port)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {注油|ちゅうゆ}: lubrication, oiling — applying oil to machinery for maintenance, not refueling",
